  "text": "Munster is a mythological region of Ireland. In the old order the island had four provinces. Leinster in the east was the province of wealth. Connacht in the west was the province of wisdom. Ulster in the north was the province of war. Munster in the southwest was the province of music and song. A fifth province, Meath, marked the center. Meath was a symbol, not a real land. Munster held the counties of Clare, Cork, Kerry, Limerick, Tipperary, and Waterford. Its valleys were rich and fertile. Its mountains were the highest in Ireland. Each range and many peaks were linked to a goddess. The Paps of Danu were two breast-shaped mountains in central Munster. Stone cairns capped them. Munster was a land of goddesses, including the Cailleach.",
